description:
Start a flag release: release a flag across environments by a flag release plan (kind "plan") or a list of environments (kind "custom"). When the user names no project, call get-projects before you ask anything. In an interactive run, confirm the project, the flag, and the plan or each environment's release with the user before you send confirm: true. When you picked the project because the user named none, name it and wait for their reply first. With kind "plan", flagReleasePlanKey names the plan (from get-flag-release-plans; default: true unless the user picks another). Prefer kind "custom" when the project has no flag release plan or none fits the request; otherwise use a plan. With kind "custom", environments lists each environment in release order. Use only immediate and policy environments. An immediate environment is only environmentKey (releaseType is never immediate). releaseType "policy" releases with the environment's default release plan, or the plan environmentReleasePlanKey names. override exists for parity with create-automated-rollout-config, but a flag release does not use it. Never make up stages, percentages, or waits: ask the user. With releaseType "policy", the environment release plan sets how the environment ramps, so tell the user when durations they asked for will not apply. waitBeforeReleaseMillis still delays an environment's start after the previous one completes. A multi-variate flag needs startingVariationId and endingVariationId (variation _ids); a boolean flag omits both (false to true). Send pullRequest (repoFullName as owner/name, and number) for a pull request's release. A webhook environment then waits for a deploy that includes the merge. Without a pull request, it starts on the next deploy signal for that environment. Returns config_id and the release as read back; manage it with the *-automated-rollout-config tools. Report all returned warnings; an environment with one is not a clean release.
Examples:
- plan, boolean flag, no pull request: {"projectKey":"default","flagKey":"new-checkout","flagReleasePlanKey":"standard","confirm":true}
- plan, multi-variate flag: {"projectKey":"default","flagKey":"theme","flagReleasePlanKey":"standard","startingVariationId":"<from _id>","endingVariationId":"<to _id>","confirm":true}
- custom, staging immediate, then production by its default release plan: {"projectKey":"default","flagKey":"new-checkout","environments":[{"environmentKey":"staging"},{"environmentKey":"production","releaseType":"policy"}],"confirm":true}

environments.description:
Only with kind custom, and required there: each environment, in release order. One example entry per release type. Omit triggerType unless the user or the flag release plan names one.
- immediate: {"environmentKey":"staging"}
- policy with the environment's default release plan: {"environmentKey":"production","releaseType":"policy"}
- policy with a named environment release plan: {"environmentKey":"production","releaseType":"policy","environmentReleasePlanKey":"prod-ramp"}
